99`t/// Editor-owned interaction contract for the top-level block drag handle.
100`t///
101`t/// The handle is row chrome: it belongs to the editor's top-level block shell,
102`t/// not to [BlockRendererBuilder] output. Keeping the contract here lets custom
103`t/// renderers rely on the same menu/reorder surface without wrapping their own
104`t/// handle, and keeps nested surfaces (table cells, inline embeds, object-block
105`t/// controls) out of row-sorting hit testing.
